1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,280
Have you ever replayed an

2
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:02,740
awkward conversation in your head?

3
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:04,640
You remember exactly what happened,

4
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:06,400
but your mind keeps searching

5
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,240
for things you could have

6
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:09,160
said differently. Maybe you wonder

7
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:10,660
whether your joke sounded strange

8
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:12,200
or whether the other person

9
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,120
misunderstood you. Psychologists often call

10
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,560
this kind of repetitive thinking

11
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:19,080
post -event processing, particularly in

12
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:20,680
the context of social anxiety.

13
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:22,460
Instead of helping you solve

14
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:24,400
anything new, your mind keeps

15
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:25,760
returning to the same moment.

16
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:27,700
The next time this happens,

17
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:29,460
try noticing the thought without

18
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:31,540
treating every imagined mistake as

19
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:33,580
a fact. A conversation is

20
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:35,100
one moment, not a complete

21
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:36,340
judgment of who you are.
